				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				84,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Fix NLS message loading and worker script execution order\n\nThe workbench bootstrap was failing with `SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<'` because `nls.messages.js` did not exist in the Sky pipeline. When the VS Code loader requested this file, the server fell through to the SPA HTML, and the browser attempted to parse HTML as JavaScript.\n\nChanges:\n- Add stub `Public/Static/Application/nls.messages.js` that seeds an empty `_VSCODE_NLS_MESSAGES` array so `vs/nls.js` falls back to literal fallback strings (the second argument every workbench callsite already passes).\n- Fix `Source/Workbench/NLS.astro` to always load `vs/nls.js` regardless of dev/prod mode; the companion `nls.messages.js` request is now served by the static stub.\n- Fix `Source/pages/Electron.astro` worker script loading: the previous bundle-mode branch collapsed three ordered scripts into one async module, breaking document order guarantees. Both modes now use separate `<script is:inline type=\"module\" src=...>` tags, ensuring browsers serialize execution in document order while permitting parallel fetch.\n\nThe workbench now bootstraps successfully in both dev and production modes.",
			"SHA": "b62c0127510bd7c79d48bef9eb46942c12d4f102"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-25T01:28:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Improve tree view data provider attachment for late-registering extensions\n\nThe original 5-retry × 150ms attachment logic (750ms total budget) times out for extensions like gitlens, clangd, and dependencies that register their views 3-5 seconds into boot.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace fixed retry schedule with exponential-ish backoff (~10s across 12 retries)\n- Add PendingAttaches set to queue views that exhaust their retry budget\n- Add RetryPendingAttaches() to sweep pending views when any successful attach occurs (indicating the workbench bridge is now wired)\n- Extract AttachToDescriptor for reuse across both immediate and pending paths\n\nThis handles the full async boot sequence where view contributions register after the initial tree-view:create event fires.",
			"SHA": "6de3a52c25e53d309283809f9dcc90b71792485d"
		},
		{
